Whether you''re a lifelong comic fan or introducing someone to the joy of newspaper comics for the first time, A Kid and A Comic offers a nostalgic reading experience filled with imagination, laughter, and adventure.', 'Various', 'Various', 'Various', 'HUM001000', 'CGN000000', 'CGN004080', 16, 'Full Color', 9.25, 12.15, 2.8, false, 1, true, 'Adventure, Fantasy, Humor', 'live', 'tbd', now(), now(), (select user_id from pg_temp.philbo_import_actor), now(), (select user_id from pg_temp.philbo_import_actor), (select user_id from pg_temp.philbo_import_actor), '14000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000114', 'PHILVIEWS #14 authorized production import', now(), '9772836924003', '{"source_file":"Philbo_August_Nov2026.csv","source_row":8,"product_slug":"phi111126207","direct_product_url":"https://philbodistribution.com/philbo-catalog/p/phi111126207","source_barcode":"9772836924003","source_printing_number":1,"imported_catalog_record":true,"authorized_import":"PHILVIEWS #14"}'::jsonb, true, false, 'https://drive.google.com/thumbnail?id=17GYsyPzw8Uxhvl-S7mjulTYaAERwVC2h&sz=w1600', null, null),
  ('58477ca9-a080-4622-abd4-3fa2b9560a31', '7b0bca08-d480-4448-af85-34a1adb1a94e', '14000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000014', 'PHI-111126-208', '79947580486120911', 'Femforce #209', 'Femforce', '209', null, 'Nightveil by Mark G. Heike, Bill Black and Stephanie Heike', 'English', 'Standard Floppy Comic', 'Ongoing', null, 'Irregular', 'T – Teen 13+', 695, 'Six distinct superhero personalities team up to fight crime and right wrongs.', 'Intriguing changes are afoot as Ms. VICTORY and hubby PARAGON stand off against a small army at sea; SHE-CAT, STARDUST and SYNN end up in the wrong place at the wrong time, and TARA gets shocking advice from her father. All this plus NIGHTVEIL in solo action solving "The Mystery of the Connelly House!" Great "good girl" art in FULL COLOR!!', 'Mark and Stephanie Heike', 'Mark G. Heike and Bobby Ragland', 'Mark G. Heike, Bill Black and Stephanie Heike', 'CGN004080', 'CGN004070', 'CGN018000', 24, 'Full Color', 6.68, 10.25, 2.4, false, 1, true, 'Superhero', 'live', 'tbd', now(), now(), (select user_id from pg_temp.philbo_import_actor), now(), (select user_id from pg_temp.philbo_import_actor), (select user_id from pg_temp.philbo_import_actor), '14000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000114', 'PHILVIEWS #14 authorized production import', now(), '79947580486120911', '{"source_file":"Philbo_August_Nov2026.csv","source_row":9,"product_slug":"phi111126208","direct_product_url":"https://philbodistribution.com/philbo-catalog/p/phi111126208","source_barcode":"79947580486120911","source_printing_number":1,"imported_catalog_record":true,"authorized_import":"PHILVIEWS #14"}'::jsonb, true, false, 'https://drive.google.com/thumbnail?id=1TBoTNiA6fKl2d5X3DWpx-zNLV4QI20Ih&sz=w1600', null, null),
  ('263f4973-1240-4969-88b1-3323439e3b9a', '1000f66e-0575-4818-9c8e-693f908f9639', '14000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000014', 'PHI-111126-209', '9781936412778', 'Alley Oop and the Mad Mod Mechanical Man', 'Alley Oop', '71', null, 'Dave Graue', 'English', 'Softcover', 'Ongoing', 'Alley Oop', 'Monthly', 'E – Everyone 5+ Suitable for all audiences', 1999, 'The continuing adventures of a time-traveling caveman!  Collecting the entire history of the famous newspaper comic strip.', 'Alley Oop meets Clank, the far-out robot! Will he be a friend of humanity... or an uncool cat? Then it’s an adventure in outer space as Alley is captured for an interstellar zoo; and there''s intrigue in the prehistoric royal courts through the chaotic misrule of Carl the First, King of Lem! Reprinting all daily strips from 1971.', 'V.T. Hamlin', 'Dave Graue', 'Dave Graue', 'CGN000000', null, null, 108, 'Black and White', 9, 8.5, 9.6, false, 1, true, 'Science Fiction, Comic Strip', 'live', 'tbd', now(), now(), (select user_id from pg_temp.philbo_import_actor), now(), (select user_id from pg_temp.philbo_import_actor), (select user_id from pg_temp.philbo_import_actor), '14000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000114', 'PHILVIEWS #14 authorized production import', now(), '9781936412778', '{"source_file":"Philbo_August_Nov2026.csv","source_row":10,"product_slug":"phi111126209","direct_product_url":"https://philbodistribution.com/philbo-catalog/p/phi111126209","source_barcode":"9781936412778","source_printing_number":1,"imported_catalog_record":true,"authorized_import":"PHILVIEWS #14"}'::jsonb, false, false, 'https://drive.google.com/thumbnail?id=1FTlcYLM8ySmBXxQweih8cZIssirjhall&sz=w1600', null, null),
  ('444cd579-baf1-4c88-a7b8-4ad4e2a9dba3', '1000f66e-0575-4818-9c8e-693f908f9639', '14000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000014', 'PHI-111126-210', '9781936412112', 'Alley Oop and the Great Moovian Migration', 'Alley Oop', '77', null, 'Dave Graue', 'English', 'Softcover', 'Ongoing', 'Alley Oop', 'Monthly', 'E – Everyone 5+ Suitable for all audiences', 1999, 'The continuing adventures of a time-traveling caveman!  Collecting the entire history of the famous newspaper comic strip.', 'Join Alley Oop on his quest for a new land when a plague of locusts ravage his homeland of Moo. This volume includes all of the daily strips from 1977—never before reprinted!', 'Dave Graue', 'Dave Graue', 'Dave Graue', 'CGN000000', null, null, 108, 'Black and White', 9, 8.5, 9.6, false, 1, true, 'Science Fiction, Comic Strip', 'live', 'tbd', now(), now(), (select user_id from pg_temp.philbo_import_actor), now(), (select user_id from pg_temp.philbo_import_actor), (select user_id from pg_temp.philbo_import_actor), '14000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000114', 'PHILVIEWS #14 authorized production import', now(), '9781936412112', '{"source_file":"Philbo_August_Nov2026.csv","source_row":11,"product_slug":"phi111126210","direct_product_url":"https://philbodistribution.com/philbo-catalog/p/phi111126210","source_barcode":"9781936412112","source_printing_number":1,"imported_catalog_record":true,"authorized_import":"PHILVIEWS #14"}'::jsonb, false, false, 'https://drive.google.com/thumbnail?id=1ggiTAbI0c0o_hFFVAHfVcm8beUBkH3J4&sz=w1600', null, null),
  ('854ce638-4f43-42e3-b12c-6203c74b9a08', '5ecd8c39-9cd6-4d71-a1a0-18576c23bb26', '14000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000014', 'PHI-111126-211', '9798988986287', 'Alpha Red #8', 'Alpha Red', '#8', null, 'James Q. Nguyen', 'English', 'Standard Floppy Comic', 'Ongoing', 'Alpha-Red-8-Star-Cross-Reg', 'Monthly', 'E – Everyone 5+ Suitable for all audiences', 499, 'This SUPER hero’s-journey follows ordinary contractor Calvin “Wes” Wesley as he finds himself called into the eternal battle between good and evil, becoming ALPHA RED!  Forty years ago, Satan was betrayed by his right-hand demon and cast into the body of a human, then cursed with immortality.  The Devil has been walking the earth for four decades plotting his revenge, but no one knows who he is or what he looks like.  Our hero gets a chip implanted in his brain that makes him super-strong, super-fast, and super-smart.  Wes must find the Enemy and stop him from taking over the world.  A cross between the Marvel Cinematic Universe, G.I. Joe, and Transformers, this story will make you laugh and make you cry.  It will have you routing for Alpha Red to find the strength to stop Satan and save the world!', 'After surviving some of his most dangerous missions yet, Alpha Red finally takes a much-needed break, joining his friend Crazy John for a night of high-flying action at a live pro wrestling event. But what begins as harmless entertainment quickly turns into chaos when a popular wrestler known as The Natural suddenly snaps, unleashing a violent rampage inside the ring—and threatening the lives of wrestlers and fans alike. When Alpha Red discovers that The Natural has been deceived into wearing mysterious wristbands that grant him supernatural strength while driving him into madness, he knows this is no ordinary meltdown. Behind the scenes, the corrupt Father Derek has orchestrated the chaos, using The Natural as a distraction so he can steal money from a charity fundraiser meant to help needy children.', 'James Q. Nguy