Comics historian Don Markstein commented that, “Some people say Mandrake the Magician... was comics’ first superhero,”', 'Volume four presents: Mandrake in North Africa (September 4 - December 23, 1939); The Mountain Bandits (December 25, 1939 - January 20, 1940); The Museum Mystery (January 22 - May 4, 1940); The Octopus Ring (May 6 - December 21, 1940); and Dr. Griff''s Invention (December 23, 1940 - April 5, 1941).', 'Lee Falk', 'Phil Davis', 'Phil Davis', 'CGN018000', null, null, 272, 'Partial Color', 12, 8.5, 48, false, 1, false, 'Action/Adventure', 'live', 'tbd', now(), now(), (select user_id from pg_temp.philbo_import_actor), now(), (select user_id from pg_temp.philbo_import_actor), (select user_id from pg_temp.philbo_import_actor), '14000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000114', 'PHILVIEWS #14 authorized production import', now(), '9781613453049', '{"source_file":"Philbo_August_Nov2026.csv","source_row":46,"product_slug":"phi111126245","direct_product_url":"https://philbodistribution.com/philbo-catalog/p/phi111126245","source_barcode":"9781613453049","source_printing_number":1,"imported_catalog_record":true,"authorized_import":"PHILVIEWS #14"}'::jsonb, true, false, 'https://drive.google.com/thumbnail?id=1r4Ii4tvNW6pWgVvEhOpK7JcWYrAgOsXc&sz=w1600', null, null),
  ('0ff7ef4a-5ea6-42e6-a549-d1814f9904af', 'b774447e-2ec1-4d57-bd06-98bea11d2b3e', '14000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000014', 'PHI-111126-246', '9781613453155', 'MANDRAKE THE MAGICIAN HC VOL 05 THE COMPLETE NEWSPAPER DAILIES', 'Mandrake the Magician: The Complete Newspaper Dailies', '5', null, 'Main cover/Phil Davis', 'English', 'Hardcover', 'Ongoing', null, 'Quarterly', 'T – Teen 13+', 6500, '"Mandrake the Magician began as a daily strip on June 11, 1934, and whether Lee Falk knew it as a sophomore at the University of Illinois, he was making history. The daily strip ended after a 79-year run, and the Sunday strip, which started in 1935, ran for 68 years. Any fan of comic strips is almost certainly familiar with Falk’s other creation, The Phantom, which started in 1936 and continues to this day.
The strips presented in this series of reprints feature two staple characters in addition to the master magician: Lothar and Princess Narda (princess of the mythical European kingdom Cockaigne). Lothar appears within the first few days (June 14, 1934), and Narda is introduced in Mandrake’s second adventure. Narda is similar to Flash Gordon’s Dale Arden: beautiful, constantly in need of rescue, and the love interest of our hero. A Prince of the Seven Nations of Africa, Lothar is Mandrake’s devoted servant, friend and companion. He is, “the strongest man in the world,” and decked out in a fez, shorts, and a leopard shirt.
Comics historian Don Markstein commented that, “Some people say Mandrake the Magician...was comics’ first superhero,” and we at Hermes Press couldn’t agree more.', '"Mandrake the Magician began as a daily strip on June 11, 1934, and whether Lee Falk knew it as a sophomore at the University of Illinois, he was making history. The daily strip ended after a 79-year run, and the Sunday strip, which started in 1935, ran for 68 years. Any fan of comic strips is almost certainly familiar with Falk’s other creation, The Phantom, which started in 1936 and continues to this day.
The strips presented in this series of reprints feature two staple characters in addition to the master magician: Lothar and Princess Narda (princess of the mythical European kingdom Cockaigne). Lothar appears within the first few days (June 14, 1934), and Narda is introduced in Mandrake’s second adventure. Narda is similar to Flash Gordon’s Dale Arden: beautiful, constantly in need of rescue, and the love interest of our hero. A Prince of the Seven Nations of Africa, Lothar is Mandrake’s devoted servant, friend and companion. He is, “the strongest man in the world,” and decked out in a fez, shorts, and a leopard shirt.
Comics historian Don Markstein commented that, “Some people say Mandrake the Magician...was comics’ first superhero,” and we at Hermes Press couldn’t agree more. Volume five presents: “The Mystery of the Striped Orchid,” 4/7/1941 - 6/21/1941; “The Great Grando,” 6/23/1941 - 11/8/194; “Lothar The Champ,” 11/10/1941 - 7/11/194; “The Rumor Factory,” 7/13/1942 - 9/12/194; and “Baron Kord,” 9/14/1942 - 4/10/1943."', 'Lee Falk', 'Phil Davis', 'Phil Davis', 'CGN018000', null, null, 272, 'Black and White', 12, 8.5, 48, false, 1, true, 'Action/Adventure', 'live', 'tbd', now(), now(), (select user_id from pg_temp.philbo_import_actor), now(), (select user_id from pg_temp.philbo_import_actor), (select user_id from pg_temp.philbo_import_actor), '14000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000114', 'PHILVIEWS #14 authorized production import', now(), '9781613453155', '{"source_file":"Philbo_August_Nov2026.csv","source_row":47,"product_slug":"phi111126246","direct_product_url":"https://philbodistribution.com/philbo-catalog/p/phi111126246","source_barcode":"9781613453155","source_printing_number":1,"imported_catalog_record":true,"authorized_import":"PHILVIEWS #14"}'::jsonb, true, false, 'https://drive.google.com/thumbnail?id=1np77qGuzu_OLRHUug5tDrx1bbhAPhS4z&sz=w1600', null, null),
  ('39b31b7b-7506-4d4c-a248-b8124e402559', 'b774447e-2ec1-4d57-bd06-98bea11d2b3e', '14000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000014', 'PHI-111126-247', '9781613453308', 'A Pictorial History of Classic Nurse Paperback Covers', null, null, null, 'Classic Nurses', 'English', 'Softcover', 'One Shot', null, 'One-Shot', 'T – Teen 13+', 2999, '“Nurse Paperbacks” which boasted covers which were eye-catching and enticing. Each of these covers are little gems that present images which reeled readers in. This book chronicles these covers and presents the first pictorial history of classic “nurse” paperback covers and features an in-depth essay about the genre and profiles many of the artists involved in creating the artwork for these tomes.', 'The 1960s and 1970s witnessed upheavals in American culture, an explosion of new ideas in cinema; a renaissance in American abstract painting, and, yes, lots of semi-salacious, suggestive, and down right kitschy “Nurse Paperbacks” which boasted covers which were eye-catching and enticing. Each of these covers are little gems that present images which reeled readers in. This book chronicles these covers and presents the first pictorial history of classic “nurse” paperback covers and features an in-depth essay about the genre and profiles many of the artists involved in creating the artwork for these tomes.
Each of these covers showcase a different aspect of the genre and were created by some of the finest illustrators of the era. Each cover, many reproduced from the original paintings, show the tongue in check humor employed in the creation these pop-culturally iconic covers.', 'Zaddick Longenback ; Dan Herman', 'various', 'unknown', 'ART023000', null, null, 224, 'Full Color', 6.5, 9, 12, false, 1, true, 'Art Book', 'live', 'tbd', now(), now(), (select user_id from pg_temp.philbo_import_actor), now(), (select user_id from pg_temp.philbo_import_actor), (select user_id from pg_temp.philbo_import_actor), '14000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000114', 'PHILVIEWS #14 authorized production import', now(), '9781613453308', '{"source_file":"Philbo_August_Nov2026.csv","source_row":48,"product_slug":"phi111126247","direct_product_url":"https://philbodistribution.com/philbo-catalog/p/phi111126247","source_barcode":"9781613453308","source_printing_number":1,"imported_catalog_record":true,"authorized_import":"PHILVIEWS #14"}'::jsonb, true, false, 'https://drive.google.com/thumbnail?id=1yS3Qyto3i5ftOCU10i7mErhSS1YKLNNZ&sz=w1600', null, null),
  ('1b97db23-4fb7-4515-a02c-37d682e541b1', 'b774447e-2ec1-4d57-bd06-98bea11d2b3e', '14000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000014', 'PHI-111126-248', '9781613452004', 'The Story of the Phantom: The Complete Avon Novels Volume 1 The Ghost Who Walks 2nd ptg', 'The Story of the Phantom: The Complete Avon Novels', '1', null, 'Main cover/George Wilson', 'English', 'Prose Book', 'Limited/Mini-Series', null, 'Bi-Monthly', 'T – Teen 13+', 1499, 'This series reprints the original Phantom novels published by Avon Books. Stories cover various timelines of the history of the Phantom.', 'Here is second edition of our beloved Phantom Avon reprints, bringing Volume One back in all its purple-suited glory!   Book one starts off with Lee Falk explaining, via the twentieth Phantom, the histories of the Phantoms that came before the current Ghost Who Walks. Famed artist George Wilson (Dr. Solar, Magnus Robot Fighter, The Phantom) painted all of the covers used for the Avon series, and they are reproduced beautifully to keep all of the details from the original books intact for a new generation of fans!  This first exciting book in the series, titled “The Story of The Phantom: The Ghost Who Walks,” tells the story of the childhood and adolescence of the twenty-first Phantom. His father, the twentieth Phantom, regales the reader and young Kit Walker of the men who came before him: the fighter who beat Redbeard the Pirate, while gaining the heart of Queen Natala; the harrowing actions that the twentieth Phantom took to regain the friendship of the Rope People, and many more stories! In this opening to the series, we also meet Diana Palmer– the love of the Phantom, the woman who always can count on the Phantom to rescue her, even before he becomes The Ghost Who Walks. This thrilling beginning shows the man behind the mask, as Kit and Guran, his confident and friend, embark on the first of many adventures. Be sure to tune in, because you’d hate to come in late to this tale!', 'Lee Falk', 'none', 'George Wilson', 'FIC002000', null, null, 160, 'Black and White', 6, 9, 4, true, 2, true, 'Action/Adventure', 'live', 'tbd', now(), now(), (select user_id from pg_temp.philbo_import_actor), now(), (select user_id from pg_temp.philbo_import_actor), (select user_id from pg_temp.philbo_import_actor), '14000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000114', 'PHILVIEWS #14 authorized production import', now(), '9781613452004', '{"source_file":"Philbo_August_Nov2026.csv","source_row":49,"product_slug":"phi111126248","direct_product_url":"https://philbodistribution.com/philbo-catalog/p/phi111126248","source_barcode":"9781613452004","source_printing_number":2,"imported_catalog_record":true,"authorized_import":"PHILVIEWS #14"}'::jsonb, true, false, 'https://drive.google.com/thumbnail?id=1lbknAmB0akdYc5Rf2seHD6UFlPVqKWHT&sz=w1600', null, null),
  ('0d118e36-c0aa-46fa-a093-1a91aac38a5d', 'b774447e-2ec1-4d57-bd06-98bea11d2b3e', '14000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000014', 'PHI-111126-249', '9781613451182', 'The Story of the Phantom: The Complete Avon Novels Volume 2 The Slave Market of Mucar', 'The Story of the Phantom: The Complete Avon Novels', '2', null, 'George Wilson', 'English', 'Prose Book', 'Limited/Mini-Series', null, 'Bi-Monthly', 'T – Teen 13+', 1499, 'This series reprints the original Phantom novels published by Avon Books. Stories cover various timelines of the history of the Phantom.', 'The Avon edition of The Phantom is back in print! This exciting installment, Volume 2 offers the classic Lee Falk tale: ""The Slave Market of Mucar.""  Famed artist George Wilson (Dr. Solar, Magnus Robot Fighter, The Phantom) painted the cover for Volume 2 as he did with all of the covers used for the Avon series, and they are reproduced beautifully to keep all of the details from the original books intact for a new generation of Phans to enjoy!  Does the ancient abomination of slavery still exist in this age of electronics? How are slaves found for this mysterious hidden market and where do they go? What is the true and amazing identity of the sinister slave dealer? Find out in this exciting second volume of The Phantom: The Complete Avon Books Volume 2!""', 'Lee Falk', 'none', 'George Wilson', 'FIC002000', null, null, 160, 'Black and White', 6, 9, 4, true, 1, true, 'Action/Adventure', 'live', 'tbd', now(), now(), (select user_id from pg_temp.philbo_import_actor), now(), (select user_id from pg_temp.philbo_import_actor), (select user_id from pg_temp.philbo_import_actor), '14000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000114', 'PHILVIEWS #14 authorized production import', now(), '9781613451182', '{"source_file":"Philbo_August_Nov2026.csv","source_row":50,"product_slug":"phi111126249","direct_product_url":"https://philbodistribution.com/philbo-catalog/p/phi111126249","source_barcode":"9781613451182","source_printing_number":1,"import