  ('fccdeb31-e2ff-47e4-998d-0fbe0786fcd2', 'c641d442-8d1a-49c3-8f7e-ebd082b33621', '15000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000015', 'PHI121626-228', '9781685248369', 'Ximphonic Versus- Consequences:IX', 'Ximphonic Versus', '9', null, 'A central glowing blue and red abstract core, a skull at the bottom, and dramatic gothic ornamentation.', 'English', 'Hardcover', 'Ongoing', 'XVNR', 'Bi-Monthly', 'T+ – Teen Plus 15+ Contains moderate violence or complex themes', 1050, 'XIMPHONIC VERSUS Dubbed "The Best Indie Comic You Haven''t Read Yet" by MSN and ScreenRant and Hailed by USA News as "The West''s Heir to ''Final Fantasy'' and ''Castlevania''s Throne," A Dark Opera, Regaling The Frightening & Shocking Tale Of Ominous Centuries Old Prince Addonnis, Who Traverses His World In Search Of An Iniquitous Power. As He Will Be Forced To Choose Between Two Evil''s And The Woman He Loves, Embarking On A Quest Of Passion & Cosmic Horror.', 'During the night''s festivities, Addonnis reveals to Sappheiros that his beloved wife has been murdered. Before Sappheiros can divulge more, an urgent message of great import comes from Addonnis'' kingdom. Suddenly he and his mentor Concerto Maestro, are abruptly called away by the stewards of their order, learning the remaining Celestial Swords have re-awoken. And their forbidden location can only be revealed by an ancient and powerful mask, known as Hi’Ramouth. Addonnis must travel to this forbidden Kingdom on a deadly quest to retrieve it unaware that these actions would set into motion a chain of events with a cataclysmic outcome.', 'S. XING XIN. B', 'S. XING XIN. B', 'S. XING XIN. B', 'CGN004360', 'CGN004370', 'CGN004380', 52, 'Full Color', 8.5, 11.25, 17.92, true, 12, true, 'Dark gothic fantasy, romance, thriller', 'live', 'tbd', now(), now(), (select user_id from pg_temp.philbo_import_actor), now(), (select user_id from pg_temp.philbo_import_actor), (select user_id from pg_temp.philbo_import_actor), '15000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000115', 'PHILVI